      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/lackland-air-force-base",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Construction on Lackland began on 15 June 1941, originally as part of Kelly Field.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lackland_Air_Force_Base",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1946 the base was renamed Lackland Army Air Field for General Frank Lackland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/lackland-air-force-base",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "When Kelly Air Force Base closed in 2001, Lackland absorbed its runway and all property west of it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
